{{/*
  ~/.config/opencode/cli.json - OpenCode 2 terminal client config.

  Kept as a chezmoi template purely so this rationale can live in the source
  without shipping to the target. cli.json is named .json, the v2 docs document
  no .jsonc variant, and the repo's check-json pre-commit hook enforces strict
  JSON, so the rendered file must not contain // comments.

  attention: v2 ships a built-in notifications plugin that raises OS
  notifications and plays sounds. Both are suppressed so the tmux pane/window
  recolor (plugin/notify.ts -> ~/.config/notify/opencode-events.sh) stays the
  single attention channel: visual, tmux-only, never popups.

  Preferred over "plugins": ["*", "-opencode.notifications"], which disables the
  whole plugin and would also take out context.attention.notify.

  plugins: disable the stock prompt footer and Copilot quota renderer, then let
  the local V2-only statusline own their presentation. The external package's
  server-side quota RPC stays active. The local plugin lives outside plugin/
  and plugins/ discovery so OpenCode V1 never tries to load it.

  Not set here on purpose:
    keybinds - v2 defaults already match nvim-cmp (ctrl+n/ctrl+p navigate, tab
               completes, return confirms, escape dismisses), so restating them
               would be noise.
    prompt.paste - a rendering setting for how large pastes display, unrelated to
               the tmux assume-paste-time fix in dot_tmux/conf.d/clipboard.conf.
*/ -}}
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/v2/cli.json",
  "theme": {
    "name": "gud-lucent"
  },
  "attention": {
    "notifications": false,
    "sound": false
  },
  "plugins": [
    "-opencode.prompt.footer",
    "-opencode-copilot-statusline.tui",
    "./v2-plugins/statusline"
  ]
}
